  "jobs": [
    {
      "id": "2424666b22a9",
      "name": "Shadow AI Update",
      "prompt": "[IMPORTANT: You are running as a scheduled cron job. DELIVERY: Your final response will be automatically delivered to the user — do NOT use send_message. SILENT: If genuinely nothing new, respond with exactly \"[SILENT]\" (nothing else).\n\nThe Shadow AI gatherer ALREADY RAN as this job's pre-step (shadow_ai_gatherer.sh — fetches Hacker News RSS, writes /tmp/shadow_ai_raw.txt, and appends raw hits to the Obsidian note 'Shadow AI Research.md' itself).\nYour ONLY job: read /tmp/shadow_ai_raw.txt and produce a <=5-bullet summary of today's hits (one line each, with links). DO NOT write files. DO NOT append to Obsidian — that is done by the gatherer. If the file says 'No matches today', respond with exactly: [SILENT]",
      "skills": [],
      "skill": "web_search",
      "model": null,
      "provider": null,
      "base_url": null,
      "script": "shadow_ai_gatherer.sh",
